Support an optional readiness pipe for service managers such as dinit and s6.
Notify only after the control socket is listening. Leave standalone startup
unchanged when TURNSTILED_READY_FD is unset.

This is a downstream patch against Turnstile 0.1.11, not yet submitted upstream.

diff --git a/src/turnstiled.8.scd b/src/turnstiled.8.scd
index efa5615..3ae0a97 100644
--- a/src/turnstiled.8.scd
+++ b/src/turnstiled.8.scd
@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@ environment variable and directory.
 
 # ENVIRONMENT
 
+*TURNSTILED\_READY\_FD*
+	If set, an inherited writable file descriptor numbered 3 or higher.
+	The daemon writes a newline and closes it after its control socket is
+	listening, before starting lingering users. Startup failure does not
+	signal readiness. An invalid value or a notification failure is fatal.
+	The variable is removed before helper processes are started.
+	If unset, no readiness notification is performed.
+
